nce: the parse ends there, queue 228)."] [206 4 "// _PyPegen_number_token: a decimal literal over sys.set_int_max_str_digits's limit, which is the run's: the"] [207 4 "// reader records the digits of one past the lowest limit (p[1]) and the error's location"] [217 21 "// a compiler's warning: PyErr_ProgramTextObject's line"] [228 1 "// compileModuleName is 3.15's compile(..., module=NAME) while that compile runs (nil: none): the warnings' module"] [229 1 "// (_PyErr_EmitSyntaxWarning's PyErr_WarnExplicitObject(..., module, NULL); queue 239)"] [232 1 "// emitCompileWarnings is _PyErr_EmitSyntaxWarning for each of the compiler's warnings, in order:"] [233 1 "// warnings.warn_explicit(msg, SyntaxWarning, file, line); a SyntaxWarning a filter turns into an error becomes"] [234 1 "// the SyntaxError of its location, the compile's result."] [280 1 "// isIncomplete reports an interactive statement that needs more lines (codeop's incomplete input):"] [281 1 "// (PY7: a fresh _IncompleteInputError each time, isIncomplete tells it)"] [297 4 "// 3.15 (queue 239): _PyEval_LazyImportName, unless the compiler forced the import eager"] [332 1 "// eagerImportName is IMPORT_NAME's eager import (_PyEval_ImportName): builtins.__import__ called, or the runtime's."] [335 3 "// builtins.__import__ replaced: called as CPython's import_name calls it"] [356 4 "// a mapping's namespace (a dict subclass's, exec's mapping; queue 219): the names stored through it"] [370 1 "// builtinImportFn is the runtime's builtins.__import__."] [373 1 "// isBuiltinImport is whether o is the runtime's builtins.__import__."] [376 1 "// builtinImport is __import__(name, globals=None, locals=None, fromlist=(), level=0)."] [415 1 "// importName is IMPORT_NAME (importlib's __import__): the module named, relative to globals' package by"] [416 1 "// level; with an empty fromlist the top-level package of the name, else the module with fromlist's"] [417 1 "// submodules imported."] [446 3 "// PyImport_ImportModuleLevelObject: an imported module's pending registration on its parent settled (3.15)"] [491 1 "// handleFromlist imports the submodules a package's fromlist names (_handle_fromlist)."] [524 5 "// _handle_fromlist: a missing submodule is skipped, unless sys.modules blocks it with None"] [535 1 "// importFrom is IMPORT_FROM: module.name, else the submodule module.name already in sys.modules (a"] [536 1 "// circular import), else an ImportError."] [538 2 "// PyObject_GetOptionalAttr: a lazy import's pending submodule by its name (suppress; 3.15, queue 239)"] [569 3 "// import_from's shadowing messages (ceval.c, queue 223): the spec's file origin, else __file__"] [589 2 "// import_from's ImportError: name the module, path its file, name_from the name (PY6b's request)"] [598 1 "// importStar is IMPORT_STAR: __all__'s names, else the module's public names, into ns."] [647 1 "// packageOf is the package a relative import is relative to (import.c's resolve_name, _calc___package__):"] [648 1 "// __package__, checked against __spec__.parent; else __spec__.parent; else, with an ImportWarning, __name__"] [649 1 "// (itself for a package)."] [709 1 "// resolveName is _resolve_name: name relative to package by level."] [725 1 "// importModule is _gcd_import: the module of the absolute name, its parents imported first."] [735 4 "// 3.15's _bootstrap calls _imp._set_lazy_attributes after a load (queue 239)"] [798 1 "// importBuiltin makes the built-in module name and puts it in sys.modules (ok false when name is not one):"] [799 1 "// the runtime's own import of them, and _imp.create_builtin's under importlib (PY6b)."] [809 23 "// a module whose Go package the host loads on demand (pyexpat)"] [812 25 "// PY6d's R5: the built-in functions' __module__"] [828 1 "// findAndLoad finds the module child (fully name) in the directories of search and runs it."] [864 1 "// loadSource compiles a module's source file and runs it as name (a package when path is not nil)."] [877 32 "// 3.15 no longer